The respondents while taking away the properties would have to resort to compromise satisfying the land losers of the lands and pay the suitable compensation in accordance with law or on the basis of consent agreed by the land losers, thereby suitably compensating for the lands having lost by the petitioners.
In the present case, the petitioners are not satisfied with the compensation paid and they have accepted some amount under protest without prejudice to their rights.
